{% comment %}
  The main review widget: summary header, star histogram, filters, review list, and the
  submission form.

  Design constraints this block is built around:

  - **Reserved space.** The container declares a min-height before any data arrives, so
    the page does not shift when reviews load. Cumulative Layout Shift is a third of the
    Core Web Vitals score and review widgets are a notorious cause of it.
  - **Deferred load.** Nothing is fetched until the widget is close to the viewport
    (IntersectionObserver). On a product page the review list is almost always below the
    fold, so paying for it during initial page load is pure waste.
  - **Aggregate from metafields.** The summary line renders server-side from
    reviews.rating, so shoppers see the rating immediately even before the list arrives.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign rating = product.metafields.reviews.rating
  assign rating_count = product.metafields.reviews.rating_count.value | default: 0

  comment
    Colour precedence, and why it is not simply "the theme block wins".

    These settings have defaults, so an untouched block still renders
    `--rm-accent: #059669` inline. The widget script only fills in a custom property that
    is not already set — so an inline value from an untouched block silently outranked
    whatever the merchant chose in the app, and Settings -> Display appeared to do nothing
    at all. That is the bug this comparison fixes.

    So: emit the variable only when the merchant has actually moved it off the default.
    Untouched, the app config applies. Changed here, this block wins — which is right,
    because the merchant is looking at a live preview of this specific placement.
  endcomment

  comment
    These must match the "default" values in the schema below. If you change one there,
    change it here too — otherwise the block starts emitting an override the merchant
    never asked for, and Settings -> Display goes dead again.
  endcomment
  assign default_accent = '#059669'
  assign default_star = '#f5a623'
  assign default_radius = 8

  assign style = ''
  if block.settings.accent_color != blank and block.settings.accent_color != default_accent
    assign style = style | append: '--rm-accent:' | append: block.settings.accent_color | append: ';'
  endif
  if block.settings.star_color != blank and block.settings.star_color != default_star
    assign style = style | append: '--rm-star-color:' | append: block.settings.star_color | append: ';'
  endif
  if block.settings.corner_radius != default_radius
    assign style = style | append: '--rm-radius:' | append: block.settings.corner_radius | append: 'px;'
  endif

  comment
    Reserved height is different: it is a layout hint about THIS placement's rendered
    height, not a style choice, so it always applies.
  endcomment
  assign style = style | append: '--rm-min-height:' | append: block.settings.reserved_height | append: 'px;'
-%}

<div
  id="reviewmaster-reviews"
  class="rm-widget"
  data-rm-widget
  data-rm-shop="{{ shop.permanent_domain }}"
  data-rm-product="{{ product.id }}"
  data-rm-per-page="{{ block.settings.per_page }}"
  data-rm-sort="{{ block.settings.default_sort }}"
  {%- comment -%}
    Where this block sits, so the app can apply the widget the merchant designed for this
    placement. Without it a merchant who built a carousel for the home page and a list for
    product pages would get whichever we guessed.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  data-rm-placement="{{ block.settings.placement }}"
  data-rm-app-url="{{ block.settings.app_url | default: 'https://reviewmaster-app.azurewebsites.net' }}"
  data-rm-allow-media="{{ block.settings.allow_media }}"
  style="{{ style }}"
  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
>
  {%- if block.settings.heading != blank -%}
    <h2 class="rm-widget__heading">{{ block.settings.heading }}</h2>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Summary block, rendered from metafields. No JS, no fetch, no layout shift.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="rm-summary">
    {%- if rating != blank and rating_count > 0 -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign value = rating.value.rating | times: 1.0
        assign full_stars = value | floor
        assign remainder = value | minus: full_stars
        assign empty_stars = 5 | minus: full_stars
        if remainder >= 0.25
          assign empty_stars = empty_stars | minus: 1
        endif
      -%}
      <div class="rm-summary__score">
        <span class="rm-summary__number">{{ value }}</span>
        <span class="rm-stars__icons" role="img" aria-label="{{ 'reviewmaster.rating_aria' | t: value: value, max: 5, count: rating_count }}">
          {%- for i in (1..full_stars) -%}<span class="rm-star rm-star--full" aria-hidden="true">★</span>{%- endfor -%}
          {%- if remainder >= 0.25 -%}<span class="rm-star rm-star--half" aria-hidden="true">★</span>{%- endif -%}
          {%- for i in (1..empty_stars) -%}<span class="rm-star rm-star--empty" aria-hidden="true">★</span>{%- endfor -%}
        </span>
        <span class="rm-summary__count">{{ 'reviewmaster.based_on' | t: count: rating_count }}</span>
      </div>
    {%- else -%}
      <div class="rm-summary__score rm-summary__score--empty">
        <span class="rm-summary__count">{{ 'reviewmaster.no_reviews_yet' | t }}</span>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if block.settings.show_write_button -%}
      <button type="button" class="rm-btn rm-btn--primary" data-rm-open-form>
        {{ 'reviewmaster.write_review' | t }}
      </button>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {%- comment -%} Histogram and filters are hydrated client-side from the API. {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if block.settings.show_histogram -%}
    <div class="rm-histogram" data-rm-histogram hidden></div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if block.settings.show_filters -%}
    <div class="rm-filters" data-rm-filters hidden></div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    min-height reserves the space. Without it the page jumps by several hundred pixels the
    moment reviews arrive, which is exactly what CLS measures.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="rm-list" data-rm-list style="min-height: var(--rm-min-height);">
    <div class="rm-skeleton" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="rm-skeleton__row"></div>
      <div class="rm-skeleton__row"></div>
      <div class="rm-skeleton__row"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="rm-pagination" data-rm-pagination hidden></div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Submission form. Hidden until requested — most visitors read rather than write, so the
    markup should not cost them anything.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="rm-form-wrap" data-rm-form-wrap hidden>
    <form class="rm-form" data-rm-form novalidate>
      <h3 class="rm-form__title">{{ 'reviewmaster.write_review' | t }}</h3>

      <fieldset class="rm-form__field rm-form__rating">
        <legend>{{ 'reviewmaster.your_rating' | t }}</legend>
        <div class="rm-rating-input" data-rm-rating-input role="radiogroup">
          {%- for i in (1..5) -%}
            <button
              type="button"
              class="rm-rating-input__star"
              data-rm-rate="{{ i }}"
              role="radio"
              aria-checked="false"
              aria-label="{{ 'reviewmaster.stars_n' | t: count: i }}"
            >★</button>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      {%- comment -%}
        Honeypot. Hidden from humans, irresistible to bots. tabindex/autocomplete off so
        keyboard and password-manager users never land in it.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="rm-hp" aria-hidden="true">
        <label>Website<input type="text" name="website" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off"></label>
      </div>

      <label class="rm-form__field">
        <span>{{ 'reviewmaster.your_name' | t }}</span>
        <input type="text" name="name" required maxlength="100" autocomplete="name">
      </label>

      <label class="rm-form__field">
        <span>{{ 'reviewmaster.your_email' | t }}</span>
        <input type="email" name="email" required maxlength="200" autocomplete="email">
        <small>{{ 'reviewmaster.email_privacy' | t }}</small>
      </label>

      <label class="rm-form__field">
        <span>{{ 'reviewmaster.review_title' | t }}</span>
        <input type="text" name="title" maxlength="200">
      </label>

      <label class="rm-form__field">
        <span>{{ 'reviewmaster.review_body' | t }}</span>
        <textarea name="body" required rows="5" maxlength="5000"></textarea>
      </label>

      {%- if block.settings.allow_media -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          The browser's native file input renders an unstyleable "Choose files / No file
          chosen" button whose text cannot be changed. The standard fix: visually hide the
          input and drive it from a styled <label>, which is still fully keyboard- and
          screen-reader-accessible because the label is bound to the input.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="rm-form__field">
          <span>{{ 'reviewmaster.add_photos' | t }}</span>
          <label class="rm-file">
            <input type="file" name="media" accept="image/*,video/*" multiple class="rm-file__input" data-rm-file>
            <span class="rm-file__btn">{{ 'reviewmaster.choose_files' | t }}</span>
            <span class="rm-file__name" data-rm-file-name>{{ 'reviewmaster.no_file' | t }}</span>
          </label>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      <div class="rm-form__actions">
        <button type="submit" class="rm-btn rm-btn--primary">{{ 'reviewmaster.submit' | t }}</button>
        <button type="button" class="rm-btn rm-btn--ghost" data-rm-cancel-form>{{ 'reviewmaster.cancel' | t }}</button>
      </div>

      <p class="rm-form__status" data-rm-form-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
    </form>
  </div>
</div>

{%- comment -%}
  No manual <script> tag here: declaring "javascript" in the block schema below makes
  Shopify load the asset from its CDN, deduplicated across blocks and after the theme's
  own scripts. Adding a tag as well double-loads it.
{%- endcomment -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Product reviews",
  "target": "section",
  "stylesheet": "reviewmaster.css",
  "javascript": "reviewmaster.js",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Customer reviews" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "app_url",
      "label": "App URL",
      "default": "https://reviewmaster-app.azurewebsites.net",
      "info": "Leave as-is unless you run ReviewMaster on a custom domain."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "placement",
      "label": "This block is on",
      "default": "product_page",
      "info": "Tells ReviewMaster which of your saved widgets to use here. Design widgets in the app under Widgets.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "product_page", "label": "Product page" },
        { "value": "collection_page", "label": "Collection page" },
        { "value": "home_page", "label": "Home page" },
        { "value": "all_pages", "label": "Anywhere" },
        { "value": "custom", "label": "Custom position" }
      ]
    },
    { "type": "color", "id": "accent_color", "label": "Accent colour", "default": "#059669" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "star_color", "label": "Star colour", "default": "#F5A623" },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "corner_radius",
      "label": "Corner radius",
      "min": 0, "max": 24, "step": 2, "unit": "px", "default": 8
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "per_page",
      "label": "Reviews per page",
      "min": 3, "max": 25, "step": 1, "default": 5,
      "info": "Pagination appears once there are more reviews than this. Existing blocks keep whatever was saved when they were added — set it here to change it."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "default_sort",
      "label": "Default sort",
      "default": "recent",
      "options": [
        { "value": "recent", "label": "Most recent" },
        { "value": "highest", "label": "Highest rating" },
        { "value": "lowest", "label": "Lowest rating" },
        { "value": "helpful", "label": "Most helpful" }
      ]
    },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_histogram", "label": "Show rating breakdown", "default": true },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_filters", "label": "Show filters", "default": true },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_write_button", "label": "Show 'Write a review' button", "default": true },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "allow_media", "label": "Allow photo and video uploads", "default": true },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "reserved_height",
      "label": "Reserved height",
      "min": 100, "max": 800, "step": 50, "unit": "px", "default": 300,
      "info": "Space held before reviews load, to prevent the page jumping. Set close to the typical rendered height."
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
